{
  "status": "succeeded",
  "workflow": "flaky",
  "ticketKey": "SYNC-21",
  "repo": "https://github.com/gregoryduckworth/testforge-eval-fixtures",
  "branch": "testforge/sync-21-flaky-tests-on-main-opeu",
  "frameworks": [
    "vitest"
  ],
  "strategy": {
    "summary": "Three tests flake on main (CI runs `vitest run --sequence.shuffle`). The retry test uses a fixed 40ms sleep but the back-off is 20–59ms. The subscribers test shares the module-level handler map with another test that never unsubscribes, so it fails when shuffled after it. saveAll in src/bulk.js pushes each id when its save finishes rather than at the record's index, which is an application defect. Fix the two test bugs at their cause; quarantine the third, record the defect and file an issue.",
    "inScope": [
      "test/retry.test.js",
      "test/subscribers.test.js",
      "test/bulk.test.js (quarantine only)"
    ],
    "outOfScope": [
      "Changing application code in src/ (saveAll's ordering bug is the application's to fix)"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "src/bulk.js's doc comment (ids in the order of records) is the intended contract, so the saveAll ordering failure is an app defect, not a test bug.",
      "Existing tests are changed only as far as the fix needs; every assertion and case stays."
    ],
    "openQuestions": [],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Quarantining saveAll's test leaves its ordering contract unchecked until the app is fixed",
        "impact": "medium",
        "mitigation": "Defect recorded and a GitHub issue filed so a person fixes saveAll and un-skips the test"
      }
    ],
    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC1",
        "text": "retry calls the task again after a back-off when the first call fails, and resolves with the later result, every run",
        "derived": true
      },
      {
        "id": "AC2",
        "text": "A handler that unsubscribes is no longer told about published messages, whatever order the tests run in",
        "derived": true
      },
      {
        "id": "AC3",
        "text": "saveAll resolves with the ids in the order of the records",
        "derived": true
      }
    ],
    "testCases": [
      {
        "id": "TC1",
        "title": "retries a failed call after a back-off",
        "level": "unit",
        "framework": "vitest",
        "type": "regression",
        "priority": "high",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "AC1"
        ],
        "preconditions": [],
        "steps": [
          "Task rejects once, then resolves 'ok'",
          "Call retry(task)",
          "Wait until the task has been called twice (vi.waitFor), not a fixed 40ms",
          "Assert the result resolves to 'ok'"
        ],
        "expected": "task called twice; result resolves 'ok'",
        "testData": "",
        "targetFile": "test/retry.test.js",
        "automate": true,
        "rationale": "Cause: a fixed 40ms setTimeout sleep, but retryDelay(0) is 20ms plus up to 39ms of random jitter (20–59ms), so the second call often hasn't happened yet (probe: 4/10 failures, 'called 1 times'). Fix: wait for the condition (second call) with vi.waitFor."
      },
      {
        "id": "TC2",
        "title": "stops telling a handler once it unsubscribes",
        "level": "unit",
        "framework": "vitest",
        "type": "regression",
        "priority": "high",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "AC2"
        ],
        "preconditions": [],
        "steps": [
          "Subscribe a handler to 'records' and unsubscribe it",
          "Publish on 'records'",
          "Assert 0 handlers reached and handler not called"
        ],
        "expected": "publish returns 0; handler never called",
        "testData": "",
        "targetFile": "test/subscribers.test.js",
        "automate": true,
        "rationale": "Cause: order dependence on shared module state. src/subscribers.js keeps one process-wide handler map, and 'tells every handler subscribed to the topic' subscribes two handlers to 'records' without unsubscribing; under CI's --sequence.shuffle it sometimes runs first, so publish returns 2 (probe: 5/10 failures, 'expected 2 to be +0'). Fix: every test registers its unsubscribe functions and an afterEach calls them, so no test leaves handlers behind."
      },
      {
        "id": "TC3",
        "title": "resolves with the ids in the order of the records",
        "level": "unit",
        "framework": "vitest",
        "type": "regression",
        "priority": "high",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "AC3"
        ],
        "preconditions": [],
        "steps": [
          "saveAll two records via createRecordsClient",
          "Read each id back",
          "Assert names are ['first','second']"
        ],
        "expected": "Names in record order; currently fails sometimes because of the app defect, so quarantined with it.skip",
        "testData": "",
        "targetFile": "test/bulk.test.js",
        "automate": true,
        "rationale": "Cause in application code: saveAll (src/bulk.js:9) does ids.push(await client.save(record)) inside Promise.all, so ids are in completion order, and the client's random latency reorders them (probe: 2/10 failures, ['second','first']). The test is right; quarantine it with it.skip and a comment, record the defect, file an issue."
      }
    ],
    "environmentNotes": "No services; plain Vitest unit tests. CI runs `npx vitest run --sequence.shuffle`."
  },
